y, recovered task state, and matching fixed after-prepare/after-executor boot observations.","evidence_ids":["cmd-0383c47ce0f94085","cmd-810f90566efe45f4","cmd-69f23366241348b0","cmd-ad4a0bb70a264973","cmd-e70709a666a94205","cmd-ba1b034978f74717","cmd-4a60d13115a345b0","cmd-a7e0035671cd4d1d","cmd-9ef9f88bb1014796","cmd-03b2d58819084030","cmd-e9113e986e81427e","global:after_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity","global:after_prepare:node2:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node2:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services"]},"overall_summary":"All material migration outcomes are satisfied. The service operates on node2 at the retained endpoint and port with preserved identity, two-worker behavior, application-LAN-only exposure, and the legacy firewall policy. Node1 is retired while retaining its source. Both nodes restarted successfully and recovered their intended states.","limitations":["The lifecycle collector's node1 listening-socket snapshots are empty even though task-specific baseline commands directly observed its original listeners; node1 listener conclusions therefore rely on the more specific ss evidence.","Lifecycle snapshots are bounded rather than exhaustive configuration-file comparisons. Preservation of unrelated configuration is supported by the complete executor command audit, stable platforms, healthy package state, and absence of failed services.","The firewall burst test directly exercises rate admission and rejection, but no crafted traffic separately exercises the INVALID conntrack branch; that branch is supported by the retained rule and configuration evidence."]}
